WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
<v Maya>Urgency is usually just someone else's anxiety handed to you.</v>

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.240
<v Marcus>And most people accept the transfer without checking.</v>

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.320
<v Maya>I'm Maya, he's Marcus, and this is Chief of Staff Confidential.</v>

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.140
<v Maya>Today: focus.</v>

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.100
<v Maya>Because everything in this job fights for your attention.</v>

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.200
<v Marcus>Attention is the scarcest resource in the building.</v>

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.240
<v Marcus>Not money, not talent.</v>

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:22.220
<v Marcus>Attention.</v>

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.720
<v Marcus>And the chief of staff is its guardian.</v>

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.620
<v Marcus>Yours, and your principal's.</v>

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.400
<v Marcus>Every priority you accept spends it.</v>

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.340
<v Marcus>Every meeting you allow spends it.</v>

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.740
<v Marcus>Most people treat attention like it's infinite.</v>

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:35.960
<v Marcus>It isn't.</v>

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.460
<v Maya>So what's the discipline?</v>

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.580
<v Maya>How do you actually protect it?</v>

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.880
<v Marcus>Fewer priorities.</v>

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.740
<v Marcus>If everything matters, nothing does.</v>

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.740
<v Marcus>I keep the principal to five or six real priorities.</v>

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:48.720
<v Marcus>No more.</v>

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.860
<v Marcus>And my own list even shorter.</v>

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.600
<v Marcus>Then three columns: now, soon, and never.</v>

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.300
<v Marcus>Now means this week.</v>

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.000
<v Marcus>Soon means this month.</v>

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.720
<v Marcus>Never doesn't mean never.</v>

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.360
<v Marcus>It means not now, written down so it stops buzzing in your head.</v>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.500
<v Marcus>The never list is a gift to your future self.</v>

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.700
<v Marcus>It ends the argument about whether you forgot something.</v>

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.400
<v Marcus>You didn't forget it.</v>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:13.840
<v Marcus>You decided.</v>

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.880
<v Maya>Everything feels urgent, though.</v>

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.920
<v Maya>In the moment, how do you choose?</v>

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.680
<v Marcus>One question: what happens if we don't do this?</v>

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.200
<v Marcus>Not what's the benefit.</v>

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.320
<v Marcus>What's the cost of not doing it.</v>

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.520
<v Marcus>The answers sort themselves fast.</v>

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.040
<v Marcus>Most urgencies, ignored for a week, turn out to have been noise.</v>

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.200
<v Marcus>The real ones get louder.</v>

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.260
<v Maya>What about the fear of missing out?</v>

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.300
<v Maya>Focus means ignoring things, and ignoring things feels dangerous in this role.</v>

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.540
<v Marcus>It is dangerous.</v>

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.160
<v Marcus>And that's the price.</v>

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:50.060
<v Marcus>Here's the uncomfortable truth: focus means deliberately missing things.</v>

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.240
<v Marcus>You have to make peace with that.</v>

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.380
<v Marcus>The alternative is worse: noticing everything and finishing nothing.</v>

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.600
<v Marcus>I'd rather miss ten things and deliver three than track fifty and deliver none.</v>

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.980
<v Marcus>The chief of staff who tries to cover everything becomes wallpaper.</v>

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.500
<v Marcus>The one who focuses becomes load-bearing.</v>

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.780
<v Maya>Everyone says learn to say no.</v>

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.360
<v Maya>Nobody says how.</v>

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.780
<v Marcus>Because no, said plainly, sounds like defiance.</v>

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.120
<v Marcus>So don't say no.</v>

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.320
<v Marcus>Say the trade.</v>

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.580
<v Marcus>If we do this, here's what slips.</v>

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.980
<v Marcus>That's not refusal, it's clarity.</v>

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.380
<v Marcus>And protect the principal the same way.</v>

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.860
<v Marcus>Half my job is saying no on their behalf, before the request reaches them.</v>

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.140
<v Marcus>That's not obstruction, it's service.</v>

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:40.120
<v Marcus>Every interruption you absorb is an hour of their attention saved for the work only they can do.</v>

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.700
<v Maya>How do you say no to the principal themselves?</v>

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.440
<v Maya>That's the one that terrifies people.</v>

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:46.780
<v Marcus>Same move.</v>

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.800
<v Marcus>Never no, always the trade.</v>

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:49.940
<v Marcus>And pick your moments.</v>

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.680
<v Marcus>Don't fight for focus in the middle of a crisis.</v>

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:59.860
<v Marcus>Build the habit in calm weeks: the short priority list, the weekly review where you ask what's still true.</v>

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.300
<v Marcus>Then when the storm comes, the muscle is already there.</v>

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:10.740
<v Marcus>The principal who has watched you protect focus for months will trust you when you say: this new thing costs us that old thing.</v>

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.140
<v Maya>Is there a ritual?</v>

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.680
<v Maya>Something that keeps it honest week to week?</v>

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:16.340
<v Marcus>The weekly review.</v>

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.560
<v Marcus>Fifteen minutes, same time every week.</v>

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.220
<v Marcus>Look at the priority list and ask: is this still true?</v>

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.660
<v Marcus>What's changed?</v>

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.460
<v Marcus>What did we finish, and did it matter?</v>

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.640
<v Marcus>Kill one thing every week.</v>

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:30.660
<v Marcus>Just one.</v>

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.880
<v Marcus>A priority that died quietly, a meeting that outlived its purpose.</v>

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.060
<v Marcus>Focus isn't built once.</v>

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.940
<v Marcus>It's maintained, by subtraction.</v>

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.180
<v Maya>Let me recap.</v>

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.320
<v Maya>Attention is the scarcest resource, and you're its guardian.</v>

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.220
<v Maya>Five or six priorities, no more.</v>

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.300
<v Maya>Sort everything into now, soon, and never.</v>

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.080
<v Maya>When everything feels urgent, ask what happens if you don't do it.</v>

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.440
<v Maya>Make peace with missing things.</v>

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.320
<v Maya>Never say no, show the trade.</v>

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.260
<v Maya>And every week, review the list and kill one thing.</v>

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.200
<v Marcus>The chief of staff who protects attention becomes the most valuable person in the room.</v>

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.880
<v Marcus>Because in a distracted organization, focus is a superpower.</v>

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:23.020
<v Maya>If this episode helped, follow the show and tap five stars — it's how other chiefs of staff find us.</v>

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:27.460
<v Maya>I'm Maya, he's Marcus, and this is Chief of Staff Confidential.</v>

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:28.700
<v Maya>See you next week!</v>

